/target

# Rust build lockfile — this crate is a library, so we do not commit
# its lockfile. Anchored to the crate root so the library's Cargo.lock
# stays untracked while `fuzz/Cargo.lock` (conventional for a
# cargo-fuzz crate, a separate non-published binary member) can be
# committed. See
# https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/faq.html#why-do-binaries-have-cargolock-in-version-control-but-not-libraries
/Cargo.lock
